{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310615,"nonce":"J77q8rHv3DOUdvjMfsbTF885/8k=","title":"Cross-file method dispatch SIGILL — forward-ref stubs created by register_stdlib_mir_forward_ref need post-load fixup against ...","message":"When `Caller.hx` is lowered during the `load_imports_efficiently` retry pass before `Holder.hx`'s real `findMeta` MIR exists, the dispatch site in `hir_to_mir.rs` falls through to `register_stdlib_mir_forward_ref(qualified_name, …)` and emits `CallDirect(stub_id)`. The stub is a real `IrFunction` (empty body, single block, `Unreachable` terminator) registered in `module.functions` so its `func_id` is valid — it's a placeholder, not callable.\n\nThe original `fixup_stale_cross_module_refs` only rewrote calls whose `func_id` was missing from any merged module, so stub-targeting calls slipped through merge and lowered to `ud2` / SIGILL at runtime.\n\nFixed commit `1c97d05` (`fix(compilation): redirect forward-ref stubs to real impls in cross-module fixup`): the fixup now walks every function looking for empty-stub patterns (`cfg.blocks.len() == 1 \u0026\u0026 all blocks empty + Unreachable`), keys them by `qualified_name.unwrap_or(name)` (stubs have `qualified_name: None` and store FQN in `name`), and rewrites every `CallDirect`/`FunctionRef`/`MakeClosure` against them to the real impl from `stdlib_function_name_map` when present.\n\n**Why:** Crossing the cache + retry-pass + multi-file dependency boundary in `load_imports_efficiently` means dispatch targets can be lowered before their providers exist. Inline name-based fixup post-merge is the only safe resolution.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- If a cross-file method call SIGILLs but `RAYZOR_RAW_MIR=1` shows a `CallDirect` to a stub, this is the path that should be resolving it.\n- If a forward-ref's qualified name has no entry in `stdlib_function_name_map` (e.g. inline-only methods like `Bytes.getUInt16`), the call stays `Unreachable` and faults at runtime — same-name lookup prevents wrong-function dispatch but cannot conjure a missing impl.\n- Related: [[feedback-no-silent-dispatch-fallthrough]] enforces that FQN-resolution must error rather than misroute.\n\n**Known remaining gap (2026-05-23):** `nue/examples/llama-smoke` clears all GGUFReader cross-file dispatches but SIGILLs inside `GGUFTokenizer.build` — likely an inline method (`Bytes.getUInt16`) failing to inline at the call site, falling through to forward-ref, then staying unresolved because no MIR impl exists under that qualified name.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_forward_ref_stub_unresolved` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}